{"path":"results/simple-ideas-6x8-p2-len3g2-comp0-7-bounties-from-3-alpha-beta-20261023/summary.md","title":"Bounties from level 3 on the default graph: α × β","html":"<h1>Bounties from level 3 on the default graph: α × β</h1>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> With bounties on every level from 3 up (not just the top), how do α and β decide how far a society gets?</p>\n<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Best overall: α = 1, β = 1. Against traditional, clearly better on hardest level, targets solved, bounty value, ROI, knowledge found (bits), knowledge per unit of money, money to the main level and waste. (8 measures; a clear difference is more than 2.7 standard errors.)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>hardest level: 6.00 against traditional 5.10, clearly better.</li>\n<li>targets solved: 7.98 against traditional 5.20, clearly better.</li>\n<li>bounty value: 477 against traditional 221, clearly better.</li>\n<li>ROI: 1.09 against traditional 0.20, clearly better.</li>\n<li>knowledge found (bits): 109 against traditional 83, clearly better.</li>\n<li>knowledge per unit of money: 0.24 against traditional 0.07, clearly better.</li>\n<li>money to the main level: 297 against traditional 964, clearly better.</li>\n<li>waste: 0.26 against traditional 0.66, clearly better.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img src=\"files/results/simple-ideas-6x8-p2-len3g2-comp0-7-bounties-from-3-alpha-beta-20261023/figures/compare.svg\" alt=\"Bounties from level 3 on the default graph: α × β\"></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>society</th>\n<th>frontier</th>\n<th>targets solved</th>\n<th>value gained</th>\n<th>ROI (value per spend)</th>\n<th>knowledge (bits)</th>\n<th>bits per money</th>\n<th>cost</th>\n<th>waste</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Traditional (α = 1, β = 0)</td>\n<td>5.1 ± 0.8</td>\n<td>5.2 ± 1.7</td>\n<td>221 ± 137</td>\n<td>0.20 ± 0.13</td>\n<td>83 ± 12</td>\n<td>0.071 ± 0.012</td>\n<td>964 ± 220</td>\n<td>0.66 ± 0.04</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>α = 1, β = 0.25</td>\n<td>6.0 ± 0.1</td>\n<td>7.8 ± 0.5</td>\n<td>460 ±